{% set listedNpcs = whileYouWereAwayNpcs or [] %}
{% from "_includes/while-you-were-away-update-schema.njk" import characterUpdateSchema %}
<task>Resolve what changed while the player was away, then follow the arrival-narration requirement below.</task>
{% include "_includes/while-you-were-away-prose-guidance.njk" %}

{% for npc in listedNpcs %}For {{ npc.name }} (last seen {{ npc.lastSeenTimeAgo }} at {{ npc.lastSeenLocationName | default(npc.last_seen_location, true) }}), return exactly one complete <characterUpdate> XML block using this canonical schema:
{{ characterUpdateSchema(npc.name) }}
Use one <needBarEffect> per applicable need bar; omit <needBarChanges> or leave it empty if none apply. Omit <travelDestination> when they stayed here. The <update> field is always required.

{% llmparse('while_away_character_update', npc.name) %}
{% endfor %}

{% if whileAwayArrivalCandidateNames | length %}
Select additional existing characters physically at the exact current location now for reunion updates; someone merely nearby or in another room does not qualify. Player, party, and already-listed characters are excluded from this roster. Use the supplied story and scene context to decide who is present.
{% for npc in whileAwayArrivalCandidates %}- {{ npc.name | escape }}{% if npc.locationName %} (recorded location: {{ npc.locationName | escape }}){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
Return <selectedCharacters><name>exact selected NPC name</name></selectedCharacters>, repeating name for each selection, or <selectedCharacters/> when none qualify. This step selects names only; individual updates follow.

{% llmparse('allowed_character_selection', whileAwayArrivalCandidateNames, 0, whileAwayArrivalCandidateNames.length) as whileAwayArrivalNames %}
{% else %}
{% set whileAwayArrivalNames = [] %}
{% endif %}

{% for name in whileAwayArrivalNames %}
For {{ name | escape }}, return exactly one complete arrival update using this self-contained canonical schema. The name is fixed and travelDestination is literal HERE because this selected character is physically at the exact current location. Use one needBarEffect per applicable bar; omit needBarChanges or leave it empty when none apply. Include the hidden update paragraph.
{{ characterUpdateSchema(name, true) }}

{% llmparse('while_away_arrival_update', name) %}
{% endfor %}

Identify only existing items/scenery that moved with the player or party from the previous location. Return one <itemSceneryMoves> XML block containing exact <itemName> values; leave it empty when none moved.

{% llmparse('exact_xml_root', 'itemSceneryMoves', { allowEmptyRoot: true }) %}

Plan what the player can directly see, learn, or experience on return. Do not expose the hidden character updates as omniscient narration.

{% llm_dummy_action %}

{% if whileAwayVisibleProseRequired %}
Draft Response: This arrival has no other narration. Write a few non-empty return-scene paragraphs from the player's perspective. Do not treat the movement notice as prior arrival prose. Output prose only.

{% llmparse('player_action_required_prose') as whileAwayPlayerProse %}
{% else %}
Draft Response: Write only new player-facing return information. Compare against the immediately preceding player-action response in THIS turn; omit its arrival descriptions, dialogue, actions, and reveals even if you could paraphrase them. If everything useful was already covered, return exactly N/A. Do not invent filler or a new event merely to avoid duplication. Otherwise output prose only.

{% llmparse('player_action_optional_prose') as whileAwayPlayerProse %}
{% endif %}

{% if whileAwayPlayerProse %}
{% set tinyBrainOptionalProseRevision = not whileAwayVisibleProseRequired %}
{% set tinyBrainAuditFocus = 'Player-facing prose must not expose hidden/offscreen knowledge; exact-location arrivals must not include nearby or party characters; structured changes must not contradict the staged update blocks. Compare the draft with the immediately preceding player-facing player-action response in THIS turn in the supplied story history. Repeated arrival descriptions, dialogue, actions, and reveals must be omitted even when paraphrased: semantic repetition is a problem, not only verbatim duplication. Keep only new observable changes, discoverable offscreen consequences, or new reunion information; do not invent filler or new events merely to avoid duplication. A bare arrival with no other narration still requires non-empty arrival prose.' %}
{% include "_includes/tinybrain-prose-audit.njk" %}
{% endif %}

{% llmresult('while_away_result') %}
